UNIT_ID: U-006
NAME: Grounding Gap — LLMs Generate Fewer Grounding Acts Than Humans
LENS: LENS_KNOWLEDGE
TYPE: evidence_result
STATUS: SOURCE_SUPPORTED
FUNCTION: Quantitative discrepancy między ludźmi a LLM w generowaniu grounding acts: LLM generuje średnio 77.5% mniej grounding acts niż ludzie w symulowanych rozmowach; poor human-LM agreement (Cohen κ) across models i datasets.
MINIMAL_FORM:
  - simulation method: LM(C_{1..t-1}) generates counterfactual message g_t for each human utterance u_t
  - metrics: base rate (frequency of grounding acts) and Cohen κ (agreement between human and LM grounding strategies)
  - result: LLM generations 77.5% less likely to contain grounding acts than humans; κ poor to fair across all models
